# VrindaVaani Custom Project Rules

This file documents the strict guidelines, constraints, and professional standards for the VrindaVaani codebase. All AI coding assistants MUST strictly adhere to these rules.

---

## 1. Visual & Graphic Standards
- **Canvas Static Backdrop Fallbacks**: Every theme registered in the settings context must map to a corresponding static/vector drawing routine inside `CelestialParticles.js` to ensure there are no empty/blank backdrops.
- **CPU-Friendly Dynamic Waves**: Any fluid, wave, or particle movement animation drawn in real-time loops must limit canvas recalculations by using coarse step widths (e.g., `x += 15` intervals) instead of pixel-by-pixel increments to maintain high framerates on low-end mobile devices.
- **Rich & Modern Aesthetics**: UIs must feel premium, modern, and trendy. Avoid raw browser defaults or generic colors. Use HSL-tailored palettes, smooth transitions, glassmorphic textures, and subtle micro-animations.

---

## 2. Performance & App Development
- **Multi-Device Compatibility**: Apps must be fully optimized to run flawlessly from low-end to high-end mobile devices. There must be zero runtime lag, flicker, or visual stuttering.
- **Cache-First (SWR) Architectures**: Implement local caching systems (e.g., synchronous local/context reads combined with asynchronous background revalidation) to ensure instant page navigation and prevent layout shifts/skeleton loader flickers.

---

## 3. Engineering & Clean Builds
- **Zero Warnings Compiler Guarantee**: At the end of every update, verify that the project builds completely clean. There must be **zero** compilation errors, warnings, or ESLint issues.
- **UI/UX Prototyping**: When creating new user interfaces, utilize Stitch tool integrations to design and verify templates before custom styling.
- **Token Efficiency**: Work efficiently and minimize token overhead by avoiding redundant operations or overly verbose subagents.
- **No Unused Variables**: Do not leave unused imports, variables, or timers in React hooks/useEffect cleanups.
- **Zero-Warning Code Quality Enforcement**: Ensure that no unused imports or variables remain in modified files before running build commands, as all ESLint warnings must be pre-resolved in the code rather than ignored.
- **Node/CommonJS Path Isolation**: When executing build-time Node.js helper scripts, always resolve database metadata modules from `/api` or CommonJS targets, to avoid typeless package ES-Module re-parsing overhead.

---

## 4. SEO & Crawlability
- **NoScript Warning Policy**: Never include functional warning phrases (e.g., 'JavaScript required' or 'Please enable JavaScript') in the `<noscript>` tags or pre-rendered headers, to prevent search engines from extracting technical fallbacks as search snippets.

---

## 5. Database & Multi-Repo Schema Synchronization
- **Cross-Component Schema Audits**: When updating database schemas, always perform a search/grep across all linked client applications (e.g. Flutter mobile apps, Next.js web frontends) to ensure database models are fully unified and do not leave out client-required columns.
- **Unified Data Seeding Checklists**: Keep a centralized SQL directory representing the unified database state to make sure schema alterations and seeding are run as cohesive operations across backend and client repos.
